{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-9669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2k+1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2k+1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2k+1 & k \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}2k+1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3-0)-(2k+1-k)-4(0-3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-(k+1)-4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6-k-1+12 \\\\  & =17-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17-k & =0 \\\\ k & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=17.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a73242ecd7ed590bf056c7669b70e01b3096d8fc1d262d117df45a05c5916e88"} {"question" "q-9669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "17"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\n- $det(F)=0$\n- $F$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(F)=-2$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-1(24-30)+2(21-24) \\\\  & =0-1\\cdot (-6)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6-6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a73242ecd7ed590bf056c7669b70e01b3096d8fc1d262d117df45a05c5916e88"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-9838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\n- $det(F)=-7$\n- $F$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(F)=-2$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-8|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2-3)-8(-1-5)+3(-3-10) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-8\\cdot (-6)+3\\cdot (-13) \\\\  & =-2+48-39 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=7$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a73242ecd7ed590bf056c7669b70e01b3096d8fc1d262d117df45a05c5916e88"} {"question" "q-128478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None of the given statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128478" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand $det(C)=28,$ find the value of $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}q & 5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (q+25)-3\\cdot (-1)+5 \\\\  & =2q+58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $28,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q+58 & =28 \\\\ 2q & =-30 \\\\ q & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a73242ecd7ed590bf056c7669b70e01b3096d8fc1d262d117df45a05c5916e88"} {"question" "q-128502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-128502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-130575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-48$, find all the possible values of $z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-130575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & z \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ z & 1\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ z & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3+z)-(2-{z}^{2})+5(-2-3z) \\\\  & =6+2z-2+{z}^{2}-10-15z \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-13z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-48,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-13z-6 & =-48 \\\\ {z}^{2}-13z+42 & =0 \\\\ z & =\\frac{-(-13)\\pm \\sqrt{{13}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 42}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm \\sqrt{1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm 1}{2} \\\\  & =6,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=6$ and $z=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-130575" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a73242ecd7ed590bf056c7669b70e01b3096d8fc1d262d117df45a05c5916e88"} {"question" "q-130575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-130575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-2$ and $3$ only"] ["text" "$3$  only"] ["text" "$5$ and $-5$ only"] ["text" "$5$ and $6$ only"] ["text" "$6$ and $7$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013865/state.json" "file_sha256" "b39e38c1819e8465e489a84006aa4a5e3be3f9e2b215c3ac17ea1ef3ac3f8faa"} {"question" "q-130575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$6$ and $7$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/De